b('Ex 9.3 Q16: altitude from A(2, 3) in the triangle A, B(4, −1), C(1, 2): equation and length.', 'BC has slope −1 (x + y = 3), so the altitude has slope 1: ' + N('x − y + 1 = 0') + '; length = |2 + 3 − 3|/√2 = ' + N('√2'))
b('Ex 9.3 Q17: p = perpendicular from the origin to the line with intercepts a, b. Show 1/p² = 1/a² + 1/b².', 'Line bx + ay = ab: p = ab/√(a² + b²) → 1/p² = (a² + b²)/(a²b²) = 1/a² + 1/b² ✓')

