# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Concurrency, families, loci
d.sec('9.z-concurrency-and-families')
b('Three lines are concurrent. What does that mean and how do you test it?', 'They pass through one point. Solve two, then check the third; or ' + T('the 3×3 determinant of coefficients = 0'))
b('Example 11: 2x + y − 3 = 0, 5x + ky − 3 = 0, 3x − y − 2 = 0 are concurrent. Find k.', 'Lines 1 and 3 meet at (1, 1); it must satisfy the second: 5 + k − 3 = 0 → ' + N('k = −2'))
b('Misc Q8: 3x + y − 2 = 0, px + 2y − 3 = 0, 2x − y − 3 = 0 meet at one point. p?', 'Lines 1 and 3 meet at (1, −1): p − 2 − 3 = 0 → ' + N('p = 5'))
b('Misc Q9: y = m₁x + c₁ etc. concurrent ⟹ m₁(c₂ − c₃) + m₂(c₃ − c₁) + m₃(c₁ − c₂) = 0. Idea?', 'Concurrency ⟺ determinant |m₁ −1 c₁; m₂ −1 c₂; m₃ −1 c₃| = 0; expanding gives the identity')
